WEBVTT

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:05.400
And now, match one of the third round of the West Tokyo qualifiers.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.820
Team Try Fighters from Seiho Academy Middle School versus

00:00:10.570 --> 00:00:15.870
team Angelfish, the swimming club from Chusui Middle School.

00:00:16.430 --> 00:00:21.160
The course of this battle depends on what the battlefield will be.

00:00:21.530 --> 00:00:23.520
We are loved by water.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:25.580
The battlefield will love us, too.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:29.020
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.590
<i>Field 13, Tundra.</i>

00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:37.240
We are truly loved by water!

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:39.710
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:40.810
Gogg!

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:41.400
Z'Gok!

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:42.040
Zock!

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.850
Take your mark!

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.390
If there's water, we are invincible!

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.030
The surface of the sea is frozen!?

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:02.620
President, the ice is so hard we can't go underwater!

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.090
No way!

00:01:08.570 --> 00:01:11.340
Without water, we are...

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:13.800
We are...

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:20.480
We are...!

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.340
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:57.000
Well, whatever...

00:02:57.290 --> 00:03:01.100
Anyway, congratulations on making it to the quarterfinals.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:02.370
Well done.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:04.760
I'm not really happy.

00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:05.900
I understand.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:11.870
The other team just self-destructed.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:15.040
Even so, victory is victory.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:19.790
Yuuma is right. Let's say that luck was on your side.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.870
Thank you for waiting.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:24.510
We now begin match two.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:26.560
Let's go see the battle.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.760
The winner of this match will be our opponent in the quarterfinals.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.270
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:03:35.530 --> 00:03:38.990
Team Babylonia from the Cosmo Academy's Aristocracy Department.

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:41.920
This team regularly reaches the higher rounds.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:43.750
All their machines are...

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:45.400
Crossbone Vanguard ones.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.210
Hoshino, who's their opponent?

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.080
Umm...

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:53.930
Joutou Municipal Middle School.

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:57.370
This is their first time competing in the championship.

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:01.260
The Destiny Gundam.

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.430
Mr. Ral, that Gunpla's just a straight assembly. right?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:07.720
Yes, The other machines, too.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.850
Hoshino, what do you mean?

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.420
I mean it isn't painted or customized.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:16.430
It was just assembled according to the manual.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:21.000
A Gunpla's performance is determined by how it's built.

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:26.780
But they've made it to round three using Gunpla with the lowest possible performance.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.830
Still, their opponent's the Cosmo Academy.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.700
They don't have a chance of winning.

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:36.830
As I expected.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:38.190
No.

00:04:43.310 --> 00:04:44.090
What the--!?

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:45.480
Know your place, snap-fit!

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:51.400
He's fast.

00:04:56.560 --> 00:04:57.720
He's like a boxer.

00:05:01.390 --> 00:05:02.220
Where'd he go?

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:24.170
Two down with a single blow!?

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:24.880
Amazing.

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.440
<i>Battle ended.</i>

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:32.760
The winner of match two is, Joto Municipal Middle School.

00:05:35.740 --> 00:05:36.840
He's strong.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:40.400
Instead of relying on the Gunpla's performance,

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:42.520
he won purely because of the fighter's control skills.

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:46.280
Interesting!

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.430
I wanna fight guys like that.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:56.600
They may say that "necessity knows now law", but I've take too much time.

00:05:57.040 --> 00:05:59.420
Gorou. Are you serious?

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.190
Our next opponent's on another level.

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.280
We have to do this for Mr. Shimon. Let's go!

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:12.560
Excuse us. You're the members of team Try Fighters, right?

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:13.680
Yeah, we are.

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:16.060
You guys are from Joutou Middle School...

00:06:16.060 --> 00:06:18.440
Yeah, our next opponent.

00:06:25.980 --> 00:06:27.100
We beg you!

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.210
In the next quarterfinals,

00:06:29.450 --> 00:06:32.330
please let us, Joutou Middle School, win!

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:37.950
We have... No. Mr. Shimon has...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:41.200
He has a reason he must win!

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.120
Oh, Big brother.

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:51.900
Yo.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.890
<b>Episode 7</b>

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:56.890
<b>Straight-Build Shimon</b>

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.020
Did you win the third round, too?

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.190
Of course. Who do you think I am?

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:07.610
You're a middle-school boxing champ, and the strongest Gunpla fighter.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:10.280
And you're my big brother!

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:12.120
That's right.

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.140
But it's like a dream.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:20.250
Though you're controlling it, I can't believe my Gunpla is winning championship matches!

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.400
It's too early to be satisfied. I'll bring you the champion's trophy.

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:28.830
So you build a new Gunpla for the national tournament, okay?

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:29.800
Right.

00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:32.470
Work on your rehabilitation, too.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:33.440
Right.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:40.890
Leave it to me, Mamoru.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.970
I'll win for sure!

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:55.740
The truth is, Mr. Shimon's brother is seriously ill.

00:07:56.140 --> 00:08:01.070
He's always in the hospital, and his only joy is building the Gunpla he loves so much.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:08.970
To encourage his brother, Mr. Shimon quit boxing, though he won the national tournament last year.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.260
And he took up Gunpla Battle!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.910
He sacrificed himself so that his brother's Gunpla could win.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:17.980
That's why...

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:22.440
So you're telling us to let you win?

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:25.520
Is that what you mean?

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:30.190
We know it's and unreasonable request.

00:08:30.620 --> 00:08:34.090
Mr. Shimon doesn't know that we're doing this.

00:08:34.090 --> 00:08:39.370
But after seeing what he's done for his brother, we can't help asking you.

00:08:40.910 --> 00:08:43.370
What an unfair request.

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:46.000
We have reasons to fight, too.

00:08:46.280 --> 00:08:50.170
But our reasons aren't as urgent as theirs.

00:08:51.310 --> 00:08:54.090
We can play Gunpla Battle anytime.

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:58.090
And we can enter the championship next year and the year after.

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.440
So what are you saying?

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:02.680
Are you going to lose for them?

00:09:02.680 --> 00:09:03.680
That's not what I meant!

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:09.200
But their eyes were really serious.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:14.150
You're right. It didn't sound like a lie.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:17.640
Sekai, what do you think?

00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:20.830
Sekai.

00:09:21.320 --> 00:09:22.750
Hey, Sekai!

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:25.900
Sekai...

00:09:29.420 --> 00:09:30.160
Mr. Ral.

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.240
What're you doing?

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:38.080
Miss Hoshino. Kousaka.

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.310
Sekai?

00:09:42.830 --> 00:09:44.540
What happened to them?

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.340
I see. That's what happened.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:56.860
Perhaps they're asking themselves the reason why they fight.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:09:59.900
Whether they should fight,

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:02.490
or just quit the battle.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:08.210
Even if they choose to fight, can they ignore the pangs of their conscience?

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:11.880
And if they go into battle,

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.690
What kind of resolve should they have in mind?

00:10:19.420 --> 00:10:23.180
Won't you teach them the meaning of their fight?

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.980
It's easy to give them advice.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:30.730
But that doesn't lead to progress in the truest sense.

00:10:31.530 --> 00:10:33.820
Thinking for themselves

00:10:34.170 --> 00:10:37.240
to find their own answer is more valuable.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:41.610
Even if that answer is mistaken.

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:51.100
<i>Wow, amazing! How did you build this Gunpla?</i>

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:53.260
<i>Actually, I didn't build it.</i>

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:56.090
Mamoru, who's your friend?

00:10:56.250 --> 00:11:00.510
Oh, Big brother! Look at this Gunpla. It's really well built!

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.140
That Gunpla...!

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:07.820
It's mine.

00:11:07.820 --> 00:11:10.430
You're my opponent in the next battle.

00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:13.650
I'm Kamiki Sekai of team Try Fighters.

00:11:13.870 --> 00:11:14.860
Huh!?

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.590
Why are you here?

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:18.240
I came to declare war.

00:11:18.540 --> 00:11:22.030
To your brother who built the Gunpla, and to you who'll fight with it.

00:11:22.440 --> 00:11:25.900
I declare that I'll win with...

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.170
my other self, Build Burning Gundam!

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:36.320
Very interesting.

00:11:39.640 --> 00:11:42.250
Sekai. Why?

00:11:45.100 --> 00:11:46.930
What was that about, Sekai?

00:11:47.560 --> 00:11:48.680
Why were you there?

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.100
How about you, Hoshino?

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:52.980
Eh? I...

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:56.320
I wanted to test my resolve.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:58.610
Me, too.

00:11:59.110 --> 00:11:59.860
I see.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:01.860
You, too...

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:06.870
You met his brother, and yet decided to fight after all.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:07.790
Yeah.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:17.960
You begged Kamiki Sekai and his team to lose on purpose?

00:12:18.250 --> 00:12:20.130
Why did you do that!?

00:12:20.130 --> 00:12:21.630
W-We're sorry.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:23.470
But Mr. Shimon, we--

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.260
Shut up!

00:12:24.720 --> 00:12:28.890
We don't need sympathy. With Mamoru's Gunpla. I'll definitely win!

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:33.060
But Seiho Academy isn't like our previous opponents.

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:35.810
We'll only get in your way.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.700
Don't worry about that.

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:49.240
Believe in me.

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:55.460
So please, stay by my side for a while more.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:56.630
Okay?

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.170
Yes Mr. Shimon.

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:02.300
We'll believe that you'll win.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:03.880
Yes.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:10.600
We now begin the quaterfinals of the West Tokyo qualifiers.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:14.730
Match one is team Try Fighters from Seiho Academy Middle School,

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:18.900
versus team FAITH from Joto Municipal Middle School.

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:24.030
Mr. Ral, did they find their answer in the end?

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:26.990
We'll see that when the battle starts.

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.910
Time to settle our battle, Izuna Shimon!

00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:32.490
Bring it on, Sekai Kamiki!

00:13:34.580 --> 00:13:37.620
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.840
<i>Field 12, Island.</i>

00:13:44.470 --> 00:13:46.220
<i>Please set your Gunpla.</i>

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.890
<i>Seconds out.</i>

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:01.270
Here we go, Mamoru! Shimon Izuna, Destiny Gundam!

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:02.150
Let's box!

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:11.990
So they're coming. Let's go, Gorou! Kouji!

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.370
Yes, Mr. Shimon!

00:14:11.990 --> 00:14:13.370
<b>Yes, Mr. Shimon!</b>

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.920
I also have a reason to fight!

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.920
Is that all you've got!?

00:14:28.630 --> 00:14:30.340
I'm not done yet!

00:14:34.890 --> 00:14:35.600
This guy is... !

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.900
The truth is, Mr. Shimon's brother is seriously ill.

00:14:44.570 --> 00:14:45.820
Yuu!

00:14:46.360 --> 00:14:47.740
A field-out warning?

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:48.860
Oh no!

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:56.950
<i>Field out.</i>

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.120
Kousaka's Gunpla has been... !

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:00.870
His determination wavered...?

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:05.550
Hoshino! Yuuma is--

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:06.300
I know!

00:15:09.880 --> 00:15:11.970
I'm here too...!

00:15:13.680 --> 00:15:14.890
I can't move.

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:16.390
Kouji!?

00:15:16.970 --> 00:15:18.850
Mr. Shimon, we'll leave this to you.

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:19.980
Stop it, Kouji!

00:15:21.270 --> 00:15:22.100
Please...

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:24.400
Please win!

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:26.320
Kouji...

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.830
<i>Field out.</i>

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:40.660
I...

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.040
I hesitated.

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.040
Even Hoshino has been...

00:15:48.210 --> 00:15:49.460
Izuna Shimon!

00:15:49.460 --> 00:15:50.970
Kamiki Sekai!

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.600
Jigen Haoh style!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:05.400
Senpu Tatsumaki-Geri!

00:16:01.730 --> 00:16:05.400
<i>Senpu Tatsumaki-Geri: Whirlwind Tornado Kick</i>

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.330
How dare you...!

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:30.090
Is that it?

00:16:31.630 --> 00:16:34.380
No. It's just the beginning!

00:16:36.350 --> 00:16:37.890
Jigen Haoh style!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.270
Seiken-Zuki!

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:41.270
<i>Seiken-Zuki: Holy Fist Thrust</i>

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:45.770
A cross-counter!

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:51.280
Sekai.

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.240
Sekai!

00:16:54.150 --> 00:16:55.110
Not yet...

00:16:55.700 --> 00:16:57.450
Not just yet!

00:16:57.990 --> 00:17:00.120
Jigen Haoh style!

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.290
Take this!

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.460
<i>Shippu-Zuki: Gale Punch</i>

00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.460
Shippu-Zuki!

00:17:06.460 --> 00:17:09.130
Blow away!

00:17:36.910 --> 00:17:39.410
Neither of them can use their right arm anymore.

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:42.700
Not bad.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:43.620
You, too.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.510
At first, I thought this was just kid's stuff.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.310
But now I know why Mamoru got into it.

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:08.020
That's right! This is Gunpla Battle!

00:18:08.020 --> 00:18:10.650
I'll win for Mamoru.

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.980
And for myself!

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:21.990
What!?

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:28.790
A flying arm bar!?

00:18:33.630 --> 00:18:34.920
Now it's over!

00:18:35.340 --> 00:18:37.920
Not yet! I won't let this end.

00:18:40.140 --> 00:18:43.310
I can't be finished!

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:47.520
The Destiny Gundam's broken right arm is--!

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:55.940
Sekai, move!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.700
I'm fired up, Shimon!

00:19:01.950 --> 00:19:04.620
Yeah, I don't want to finish this yet.

00:19:04.870 --> 00:19:07.080
But I'm gonna settle this!

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:09.290
My sentiments exactly!

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.880
I didn't think you'd knock me down.

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:20.340
But...

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.550
the 10-count hasn't sounded yet!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:24.550
Where did he go!?

00:19:29.180 --> 00:19:30.850
Jigen Haoh style!

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.560
<i>Senko Majutsu-Geri: Flashing Magical Kick</i>

00:19:31.520 --> 00:19:34.560
Senko Majutsu-Geri!

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.890
Big brother! How was the match?

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:10.270
We lost. I'm sorry.

00:20:10.480 --> 00:20:13.270
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

00:20:13.270 --> 00:20:16.190
I'll build a much stronger Gunpla.

00:20:16.940 --> 00:20:19.570
Like Mr. Kamiki's Build Burning.

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.780
I'll customize it and paint it too.

00:20:21.780 --> 00:20:24.320
I'll build the best Gunpla ever!

00:20:25.910 --> 00:20:28.450
Then, will you fight for me again?

00:20:28.740 --> 00:20:30.620
Yeah, of course.

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.170
I'll get better for sure!

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.040
Yeah.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:41.130
So this is where you are.

00:20:41.590 --> 00:20:42.550
Hoshino.

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.720
We got a call from Joto Middle School.

00:20:47.300 --> 00:20:50.430
I see. His brother said all that...

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:54.100
Sekai, did you this would happen?

00:20:54.390 --> 00:20:56.480
Is that why you could fight without hesitating?

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:58.020
I did hesitate.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:04.740
But when I met Shimon Izuna's brother and I saw his joyous face,

00:21:04.740 --> 00:21:07.240
I remembered something my master said.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:11.200
"Don't bring a lie to a battle."

00:21:11.580 --> 00:21:13.250
In other words, don't lie.

00:21:13.250 --> 00:21:14.120
That's right.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:19.630
If I lost on purpose, Izuna Shimon's victory would be a lie.

00:21:20.420 --> 00:21:24.300
And his brother would be delighted at that lie.

00:21:24.880 --> 00:21:28.050
I didn't want to do that. That's what I thought.

00:21:28.640 --> 00:21:29.800
I see.

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:30.510
Yeah.

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:35.060
You're pretty cool.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:36.770
Eh? What?

00:21:37.150 --> 00:21:37.810
Huh?

00:21:38.190 --> 00:21:39.360
What did you say?

00:21:39.980 --> 00:21:41.230
I said, I'm such a fool.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.190
Why are you a fool?

00:21:43.400 --> 00:21:45.150
Because that's what I am?

00:21:50.490 --> 00:21:52.620
I don't really understand.

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:54.540
You don't need to!

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:28.630
N-No way!

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.840
The Zeo Zeong I put so much effort into building is...

00:23:35.310 --> 00:23:36.680
What do you say, Mr. President?

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:39.480
Will you choose me as a member of your team?

00:23:40.140 --> 00:23:41.730
Yes, of course.

00:23:41.730 --> 00:23:44.360
Where did you get such ability?

00:23:44.860 --> 00:23:46.190
Didn't I tell you?

00:23:46.650 --> 00:23:48.940
My previous school was...

00:23:49.360 --> 00:23:51.490
the private Gunpla Academy.

00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:53.570
G-Gunpla Academy!?

00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:55.450
Last year's champion team!

00:24:00.500 --> 00:24:02.870
In the semifinals, Gyanko's team fights against...

00:24:02.870 --> 00:24:04.250
Team G-Master.

00:24:04.250 --> 00:24:05.840
The odds are against them.

00:24:06.040 --> 00:24:08.090
Next Episode, "Upon This Shied."

00:24:08.090 --> 00:24:09.420
Win this, Gyanko!
